* Roland TB-303 VCO, from the service notes (First Edition, 1982, p. 5; D275): the pitch's slide, the exponential
* converter, the saw's capacitor and its reset, the source follower and the square's shaper. The reference for
* CoolSynth 303's VCO.
*
* Rails as ideal sources: 12 V (the filled arrows), 5.333 V (the crossed circles, IC16 pin 7).
* Transistors: the 2SC945(P) and 2SA733(P) as the 808 netlists' stand-ins; the dual 2SC1583 (Q26) as two matched
* NPNs (no published model: hFE >= 500); the 2SK30(O) as an N-JFET of Idss 1 mA (rank O: 0.6 to 1.4 mA); the 1SS133
* and 1S2473 as the standard 1N4148; the AN6562 (an LM358 in effect) as a single-pole 1 MHz op-amp whose output
* swings from 0 to 10.5 V on 12 V.
*
* The CPU's note: the 6-bit ladder R74 to R90 (100k and 200k, 0.1 %) from IC10's 5.333 V buffers, one twelfth of a
* volt a step, taken as its Thevenin equivalent, the code's voltage behind 100 kOhm. The A key unshifted is code 33,
* 2.75 V (CV OUT at TUNE); the lowest C 1 V, the highest 5 V.
*
* Parameters: cv (volts at the start), cv2 and tcv (the voltage after tcv seconds), slide (1: IC12 puts C35 on the
* ladder, a 22 ms RC; 0: C35 follows IC11b's output), tm4 (TUNE trimmer TM4, 47k B, 0..1 from 5.333 V to 12 V),
* tm5 (WIDTH trimmer TM5, 4.7k, 0..1 of its resistance), tune (the TUNING knob VR2, 50k B, 0..1 from ground to
* 5.333 V; its top end read as 5.333 V), tend.
* tm4 and tm5 as calibrate.py sets them by page 7's procedure: A at 110.0 Hz, low C to high C 2:1, to high C
* transposed up 4.002:1 (with the models as fitted below).
.param cv=2.75 cv2=2.75 tcv=1 slide=0 tm4=0.5719 tm5=0.7386 tune=0.5 tend=0.05
.param rtm4a={max(47k*tm4, 1)} rtm4b={max(47k*(1-tm4), 1)} rtm5={max(4.7k*tm5, 1)}
.param rv2a={max(50k*(1-tune), 1)} rv2b={max(50k*tune, 1)}

* The 2SC945 and 2SA733 (no published models) as Fairchild's 2N3904 and 2N3906 from their datasheets, with their
* storage times and low-current gain (the reset, Q24, Q25 and Q27, a thyristor, lets go only through them), their IS
* set to both parts' typical VBE of 0.62 V at 1 mA (39 fA), the 2SA733(P)'s gain to its rank's middle (300).
.model QEM NPN(IS=39f XTI=3 EG=1.11 VAF=74.03 BF=416.4 NE=1.259 ISE=6.734f IKF=66.78m XTB=1.5 BR=.7371 NC=2
+ ISC=0 IKR=0 RC=1 CJC=3.638p MJC=.3085 VJC=.75 FC=.5 CJE=4.493p MJE=.2593 VJE=.75 TR=239.5n TF=301.2p ITF=.4
+ VTF=4 XTF=2 RB=10)
.model QPM PNP(IS=39f XTI=3 EG=1.11 VAF=18.7 BF=300 NE=1.5 ISE=0 IKF=80m XTB=1.5 BR=4.977 NC=2 ISC=0 IKR=0
+ RC=2.5 CJC=9.728p MJC=.5776 VJC=.75 FC=.5 CJE=8.063p MJE=.3677 VJE=.75 TR=33.42n TF=179.3p ITF=.4 VTF=4 XTF=6
+ RB=10)
.model Q1583 NPN(IS=10f BF=500 BR=4 CJE=5p CJC=2.5p)
.model JFO NJF(VTO=-1.0 BETA=1m LAMBDA=2m CGS=8p CGD=3p)
.model DEM D(IS=2.52n N=1.752 RS=0.568 CJO=2p)
.model DCL D(IS=1e-12 N=1)
.model SWI SW(VT=0.5 VH=0.1 RON=200 ROFF=1G)

VCC vcc 0 12
VR vr 0 5.333

* The ladder's voltage behind its 100 kOhm.
VDAC ndac0 0 PWL(0 {cv} {tcv} {cv} {tcv+1u} {cv2})
RDAC ndac0 ndac 100k

* The slide: IC12's switch 8-9 puts C35 on the ladder's output while a slide plays; switch 10-11 holds C35 at
* IC11b's output otherwise, so a slide starts from the pitch that sounds (Q29 and Q30 set the two oppositely; here
* the slide parameter does).
VSL nsl 0 {slide}
VNS nns 0 {1-slide}
S8 ndac n35 nsl 0 SWI
S10 n35 ncv nns 0 SWI
C35 n35 0 0.22u

* IC11b, a follower (R107 2.2k), its output clamped by D30 to ground and D31 to 5.333 V: the CV.
GB 0 ib ndac nm11b 1m
RIB ib 0 1e8
CIB ib 0 159.15p
BB ncv 0 V=v(ib)
DCPB ib ncpb DCL
VCPB ncpb 0 9.95
DCNB ncnb ib DCL
VCNB ncnb 0 0.57
R107 ncv nm11b 2.2k
D31 ncv vr DEM
D30 0 ncv DEM

* The exponential converter: Q26's left half sinks the reference current (R103 from 12 V, R102 from TM4's wiper)
* at 5.333 V, IC11a driving the shared emitters through R104 (C34 across IC11a); the right half's base is the CV
* through TM5 and R106 over the posistor R100 (560 ohm, taken at 25 C) to 5.333 V, and TUNING through R118.
R103 vcc nref 220k
RTM4A vr ntm4 {rtm4a}
RTM4B ntm4 vcc {rtm4b}
R102 ntm4 nref 100k
GA 0 ia vr nref 1m
RIA ia 0 1e8
CIA ia 0 159.15p
BA n11a 0 V=v(ia)
DCPA ia ncpa DCL
VCPA ncpa 0 9.95
DCNA ncna ia DCL
VCNA ncna 0 0.57
C34 n11a nref 1n
R104 n11a nem 2.2k
Q26A nref vr nem Q1583
Q26B nc33 nbase nem Q1583
RTM5 ncv n5 {rtm5}
R106 n5 nbase 27k
R100 nbase vr 560
R118 nbase ntune 100k
RV2A vr ntune {rv2a}
RV2B ntune 0 {rv2b}

* The saw: Q26B discharges C33 (0.01 uF) from about 12 V; at about 5.5 V Q25 turns on (its base at Q24's diode over
* R101 to 5.333 V), pulls Q27's base, and Q27 through D25 lifts Q24's node and with it, through Q25, C33 back up.
C33 nc33 0 10n
Q25 nb27 nb nc33 QEM
Q27 nk nb27 vcc QPM
D25 nk nb DEM
Q24 nb nb ne24 QEM
R101 ne24 vr 10k

* Q28, a source follower: the saw.
J28 vcc nc33 nsaw JFO
R105 nsaw 0 10k

* The square: Q8 (PNP), its base from the saw through R35 (100k) and, for the edges, C10 and R34 (10k); its emitter
* from 12 V through R45 (22k), held by C11 (1 uF); its collector over R36 (10k) to 5.333 V.
R35 nsaw nb8 100k
C10 nsaw nc10 10n
R34 nc10 nb8 10k
R45 vcc ne8 22k
C11 ne8 0 1u
Q8 nsq nb8 ne8 QPM
R36 nsq vr 10k

* The start: the thyristor's latched state is also a DC solution (the circuit's power-up kicks it out); the render
* starts on the ramp instead.
.ic v(nc33)=8 v(nb)=5.9

.options method=trap reltol=1e-5 abstol=1e-12 vntol=1e-7
.tran 0.2u {tend} 0 0.2u
.end
